Q: What is the capital of Australia?
A: Ask it "What is the capital of Jordan?" and it may continue with another question, as such questions often appear in lists. Instruction tuning (also called supervised fine-tuning, SFT) is fine-tuning on many examples of instructions paired with good responses, formatted consistently: The loss is the same next-token cross-entropy as in pretraining, usually computed only on the response tokens.
   sources: Chapter 25, "Instruction tuning"  (match 2.8)

